        "timestamp": 1788638484
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Not really related to circuits, but I found it cute that the <code>Program</code> type is an instance of a certain sort of \"type-level fold\":</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">inductive</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">initial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">v</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">empty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initial</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Fold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">initial</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">t</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">next</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>It is pretty neat that we can abstract such things in Lean.</p>",
        "id": 623011402,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam Schlesinger",
        "timestamp": 1789004107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I guess it isn't really a fold.</p>",
        "id": 623011493,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam Schlesinger",
        "timestamp": 1789004157
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It is more of an unfold.</p>",
        "id": 623011513,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam Schlesinger",
        "timestamp": 1789004163
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>There is a nice library lying under here where this can be the underlying data structure for a lot of different types and a lot of theorems can be proven only once in a general way.</p>",
        "id": 623012382,
        "sender_full_name": "Sam Schlesinger",
        "timestamp": 1789004645
    }
]